WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.570
(slow upbeat music)

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:02.710
- [Narrator] This Great Big Story

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:03.580
was made possible

00:00:04.505 --> 00:00:06.240
by the Singapore Tourism Board.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.520
(slow upbeat music)

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.568
- We try to push the
boundaries of which ingredients

00:00:11.568 --> 00:00:13.210
can be used in a cocktail.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:18.210
We've used ants to grasshoppers to kimchi,

00:00:18.589 --> 00:00:20.790
and we've even used salmon roe

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.594
in one of our cocktails.

00:00:22.594 --> 00:00:26.814
We are one of the only bars
in the world that focuses

00:00:26.814 --> 00:00:30.183
on using ingredients
in the way that we do.

00:00:33.674 --> 00:00:35.370
(slow upbeat music)

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.950
My name is Vijay Mudaliar,

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:38.971
and I'm the co-owner of Native.

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:41.440
We're a cocktail bar based in Singapore

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.400
that focuses

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.292
on working with foraging ingredients.

00:00:44.292 --> 00:00:47.875
(slow upbeat music)

00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:51.636
So I've been foraging for
about three years now.

00:00:51.636 --> 00:00:54.270
As a younger bartender,
I was always interested

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:57.040
in like unique imported ingredients.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.070
The environment in
Singapore is quite diverse;

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.130
sometimes we do a bit of urban foraging.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.430
We also go out into

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.560
the forested areas and we also go down

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.821
to the coastal lines to
get things like seaweeds

00:01:07.821 --> 00:01:09.789
and clams.

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:12.389
(slow upbeat music)

00:01:12.389 --> 00:01:15.780
Using some of these unusual
ingredients we can get

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.327
certain interesting flavors.

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:21.050
The forage ants, for
example, contain formic acid,

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:22.370
so when you pop them, they taste

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:25.379
like little limes or lemons
because of the acidity.

00:01:25.379 --> 00:01:28.770
For grasshoppers, what
comes out is this like miso,

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:30.480
vegemite, soy flavor,

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.230
which has a real savory note to it.

00:01:33.238 --> 00:01:36.049
(slow upbeat music)

00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:39.310
Our cocktail making process lasts four

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:40.197
to six months.

00:01:40.197 --> 00:01:44.628
It usually starts from an idea
that is based on a tradition,

00:01:44.628 --> 00:01:48.375
culture, location or the environment.

00:01:48.375 --> 00:01:51.168
For example, our Peranakan cocktail

00:01:51.168 --> 00:01:53.729
is based off the local Peranakan culture

00:01:53.729 --> 00:01:55.940
and is inspired by one of the

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:58.015
desserts called the quay salad.

00:01:58.015 --> 00:02:00.297
We use pandan and laksa leaf from

00:02:00.297 --> 00:02:03.439
a local organic farmer;

00:02:03.439 --> 00:02:05.800
a jackfruit rum,

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:08.878
so we're using foraged
jackfruit; also goat's milk

00:02:08.878 --> 00:02:11.135
from a local goat's farm.

00:02:11.135 --> 00:02:13.800
The enzymes in the jackfruits

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.966
curdles the milk, and
we get a clear cocktail.

00:02:16.966 --> 00:02:20.043
We try to incorporate those ingredients

00:02:20.043 --> 00:02:23.123
that have been used culturally
for over a hundred years.

00:02:24.888 --> 00:02:29.715
(slow upbeat music)

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:32.090
What I like about incorporating
foraging ingredients

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.548
is that it allows us to understand

00:02:34.548 --> 00:02:36.341
our environment a lot better

00:02:36.341 --> 00:02:40.213
and to find forgotten
ingredients in our culture.

00:02:40.213 --> 00:02:42.700
Hopefully in the next few years,

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.423
the idea of foraging won't feel so new.

00:02:46.363 --> 00:02:50.131
I think people want to
experience their location,

00:02:50.131 --> 00:02:52.608
and when people are traveling the world,

00:02:52.608 --> 00:02:54.579
they want to have a sense of identity

00:02:54.579 --> 00:02:56.623
at the place where they are.

